{
  "profile": "development",
  "_profile_doc": "profile: 'stable' asks at every gate. 'development' (set 2026-09-27, .claude/state/profile.log) turns every ask into an allow logged to .claude/state/guard-relaxed.log, except the asks guard.py keeps: a secret file, deleting or archiving the GitHub repository, printing a token, a search that would reach a secret file, releasing another session's fix-lock, and a command too complex to check within the guard's time budget. Denies never change. Switch with `guard.py profile development|stable`; loosening asks the owner. See guard.py's header and AGENTS.md > Claude guard and fix-lock.",
  "fix_lock_release_needs_owner": true,
  "_fix_lock_doc": "The fix-lock is opt-in (AGENTS.md > Claude guard and fix-lock; owner, 2026-10-10): nothing here forces it. fix_lock_release_needs_owner true (the default, written out so the choice is visible) means `guard.py fix-lock off` asks the owner in the stable profile; in development that ask is a logged allow. No fix_lock_preflight is set.",
  "_doc": "Policy for .claude/hooks/guard.py (see AGENTS.md > Claude guard and fix-lock). Globs without '/' match the basename; with '/' they match the repo-relative path ('*' crosses '/'). Every example below is replayed by test_guard.py: add one whenever the policy changes. guard.py/test_guard.py are identical to rikurinode's; only this file differs. secret_globs mirror .gitignore's secrets section as far as basename globs can (directories such as secrets/ cannot be expressed), plus the gh and git credential files. protected_globs are the procedure, the gates, the records that decide scope and gate status, their planned homes, and the directories that hold them (so rm -r of the whole directory asks too). funds_patterns here guard GitHub state and history changes (this repo has no money path yet); add money and execution commands when they exist.",

  "secret_globs": [".env", ".env.*", "*.env", "*.env.*", ".envrc", ".netrc", ".npmrc", ".pypirc",
                   "*.local.env", "*.local.json", "*.local.toml", "*.local.yaml", "*.local.yml",
                   "*.key", "*.pem", "*.p12", "*.pfx", "*.jks", "*.keystore", "*.kdbx",
                   "*.token", "*.secret", "id_rsa*", "id_ed25519*", "id_ecdsa*",
                   "credentials", "credentials.json", "client_secret*.json",
                   "service-account*.json", ".git-credentials", "hosts.yml"],
  "secret_allow_globs": ["*.example", "*.sample", "*.template", "*.pub", "settings.local.json"],

  "protected_globs": ["AGENTS.md", "CLAUDE.md", "REVIEW.md", ".gitignore",
                      ".claude", ".claude/settings.json", ".claude/settings.local.json",
                      ".claude/hooks", ".claude/hooks/*", ".claude/agents", ".claude/agents/*",
                      ".claude/state", ".claude/state/*", ".claude/settings*",
                      ".github", ".github/workflows", ".github/workflows/*",
                      "scripts/quality", "scripts/quality/*",
                      "deny.toml", ".gitleaks.toml", ".pre-commit-config.yaml",
                      "doc",
                      "doc/Rikuri_Pi_Engineering_Standard_*.md",
                      "doc/Rikuri_Pi_Engineering_Templates_*.md",
                      "doc/Rikuri_Pi_Foundation0_Test_Replay_and_Acceptance_Strategy_*.md",
                      "doc/Rikuri_Pi_ADR_*.md",
                      "doc/Rikuri_Pi_Foundation0_Rebaselined_Stage_Plan_*.md",
                      "docs/engineering/ENGINEERING_STANDARD.md",
                      "docs/architecture/adr", "docs/architecture/adr/*",
                      "docs/stage-gates", "docs/stage-gates/*"],

  "protected_branches": ["main", "master"],

  "test_globs": ["tests/*", "*/tests/*", "*_test.rs", "test_*.py",
                 "fixtures/*", "*/fixtures/*", "golden/*", "*/golden/*",
                 "*baseline*.json", "*baseline*.txt", "*baseline*.toml",
                 "*baseline*.yaml", "*baseline*.yml", "*baseline*.csv"],
  "_inline_tests_doc": "Tests written inside a source file are tests too. Rust keeps unit tests in a `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` block at the end of the file (11 of 53 tracked .rs files, 2026-10-10): from a file's first marker (`#[cfg(test)]`, or a test-only helper under `#[cfg(any(test, …))]`/`all(test, …)`; never `cfg(not(test))`) to its end is read-only under the fix-lock. Attribute and comment lines directly above the first marker (across blank lines) belong to it: a `#[cfg(any())]` there switches the tests off. Lines that make production code act differently under test (cfg(test)/cfg!(test)/cfg_attr(test,…), or an assert-macro shadow) may not be added, removed or changed anywhere in the file while locked. Edits there must match exactly, and shell writes to any .rs file are refused while locked (use Edit/Write). The rule is AISecurity's and rikurinode's, copied unchanged (lesson gate 2026-09-28, rikurinode docs/build-records/2026-09-28-fix-lock-covers-inline-tests.md); this repository had no Rust code then and gained the rule 2026-10-10 (docs/build-records/2026-10-10-fix-lock-covers-inline-tests.md). The inline-test examples quote crates/rikuri-domain/src/time.rs exactly: when that file changes, update them, since an old_string that no longer matches is denied for that reason instead and the example stops testing the rule.",
  "inline_tests": [{"glob": "*.rs", "starts_at": "^[ \\t\\f\\v\\r\u200b-\u200f\u2060\ufeff]*#\\s*\\[\\s*cfg\\s*\\(\\s*(?:test|(?:any|all)\\s*\\((?:.*[(,]\\s*)?(?<!not\\()test(?=\\s*[,)]).*\\))\\s*\\)\\s*\\]", "attached_above": "^[ \\t\\f\\v\\r\u200b-\u200f\u2060\ufeff]*(#\\s*\\[|//|/\\*|\\*)", "guarded_lines": "cfg(?:_attr)?\\s*!?\\s*\\(.*\\btest\\b|macro_rules!\\s*(?:assert\\w*|debug_assert\\w*|panic|unreachable|todo)\\b"}],

  "funds_patterns": [
    {"regex": "\\bgh\\s+pr\\s+merge\\b",
     "reason": "gh pr merge lands work on a protected branch on GitHub — owner approves"},
    {"regex": "\\bgh\\s+repo\\s+(unarchive|rename|edit)\\b",
     "reason": "changes or deletes the GitHub repository itself — owner approves"},
    {"regex": "\\bgh\\s+repo\\s+(delete|archive)\\b", "reason": "deletes or archives the GitHub repository — irreversible; owner approves", "always_ask": true},
    {"regex": "(?i)\\bgh\\s+api\\b(?!.*\\sgraphql(\\s|$))(?!.*(-X|--method)[\\s=]*GET\\b(?!.*(-X|--method)))(?=.*((-X|--method)[\\s=]*(PUT|POST|PATCH|DELETE)\\b|\\s(-f|--field|--raw-field|--input)))",
     "reason": "a gh api write changes GitHub state directly (branch protection is the S00.01 gate; also rulesets, workflows, secrets, merges, refs) — owner approves"},
    {"regex": "(?i)\\bgh\\s+api\\b.*\\sgraphql(\\s|$).*(mutation|--input|=@|\\$)",
     "reason": "a GraphQL mutation, or a GraphQL body the guard cannot read (file, --input, shell variable), may change GitHub state — owner approves"},
    {"regex": "\\bgh\\s+workflow\\s+disable\\b",
     "reason": "disables a CI workflow — a required gate is never switched off to get green (Law 2); owner approves"},
    {"regex": "\\bgh\\s+(secret|variable)\\s+(set|delete|remove)\\b",
     "reason": "changes GitHub Actions secrets or variables — owner approves"},
    {"regex": "\\bgh\\s+auth\\s+(token\\b|status\\b.*(\\s-t\\b|--show-token\\b))",
     "reason": "prints a GitHub credential into the transcript (gh auth token, gh auth status --show-token) — owner approves", "always_ask": true},
    {"regex": "\\bgit\\s+filter-(repo|branch)\\b",
     "reason": "rewrites repository history — owner approves"}
  ],

